page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>L-house · Connected rooms</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f3f0e8;color:#293f32;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}header,main,footer{max-width:1340px;margin:auto;padding:30px}header{padding-top:46px}h1{font:normal clamp(35px,5vw,56px)/1.08 Georgia,serif;margin:15px 0 22px}h2{font:normal 30px/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:12px 0 18px}p{max-width:900px}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:4px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase}nav,.controls{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin:22px 0}img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.controls button{font:inherit;padding:10px 22px;border:1px solid #6b806c;background:#fffdf7;color:#293f32;cursor:pointer}.controls button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#284836;color:white}.controls span{font-size:14px}section,article{margin-bottom:40px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:28px}.panel{background:#fffdf7;padding:22px;min-width:0}.callout{padding:20px 24px;background:#e9ddc4;border-left:3px solid #9c713d;margin:24px 0}.note{font-size:14px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td{padding:10px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid #d3d5c7}td:last-child{white-space:nowrap;text-align:right}ul{padding-left:20px}li{margin:8px 0}footer{font-size:14px}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ac7853;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:800px){header,main,footer{padding:20px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.panel{padding:16px}}</style><header><div class="eyebrow">L-house / Combined model / 7 October 2026</div><h1>Kitchen, dining and living.<br>One connected model.</h1><p>The approved furniture and kitchen joinery are now fitted together. Four oak-framed glass panels can close the kitchen. A short timber screen defines the living area without enclosing it.</p><nav><a href="renders.html">Kitchen furniture study</a><a href="#layout">Layout and clearances</a><a href="boot-room.html">Selected pantry plan</a></nav><div class="callout"><strong>Updated finishes: faded ivory rug, pale oak dining furniture and a earthy olive sofa.</strong><p>The dining group and chandelier move 600 mm towards the hall. The island and stools move 100 mm towards the sink and 75 mm towards the pantry wall. The hall remains a separate route. Kitchen parquet now continues through dining and living, with full-height linen curtains at the garden bifolds.</p></div></header><main>COMPARE FIGURES<section id="layout"><h2>The coordinated layout</h2><div class="grid"><div class="panel"><a href="combined-renders/plan.svg" target="_blank"><img src="combined-renders/plan.svg" width="1400" height="1050" alt="Plan with furniture footprints and measured clearances"></a><p class="note">Solid shapes show furniture bounds. Rust dashes show a 400 mm chair pull-out test. The green line is a nominal 600 mm route screening path. Sofa is shown by its overall footprint. The sampled route has only 10 mm spare at its tightest point; this needs further layout work.</p></div><div class="panel"><table><tbody>ROWS</tbody></table><p class="note">Distances are model measurements, not access certification. Chair pull-out is an allowance, not a person simulation.</p></div></div><div class="callout"><strong>Keep the rear of the stools out of the through-route.</strong><p>There is only 0.64 m behind the empty stool geometry. Seated use reduces this further. Use the side aisles and the separate hall route. The 0.50 m behind pulled-out rear dining chairs is also local seating space, not a circulation route.</p></div><h2>What still needs a decision</h2><ul><li>The glass divider is a folding proposal because the earlier sliding stack conflicted with the log-burner wall. Hardware and installation details remain open.</li><li>The pantry door swing, open appliances and occupied-seat movement need a detailed check.</li><li>The 3.2 m ceiling still needs coordination with the first floor.</li><li>The log burner remains a location study; its installation and flue are not designed here.</li></ul></section></main><footer><p>Five Blender/Cycles views from one editable scene. Frame 1 is the open divider; frame 60 is closed. The kitchen and living source files remain unchanged. No paid asset was purchased. These are presentation views, not a sunlight study.</p></footer><script>const image=document.querySelector('#comparison'),link=document.querySelector('#comparisonLink'),note=document.querySelector('#stateNote');document.querySelectorAll('[data-state]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{const state=button.dataset.state;image.src='combined-renders/dining-kitchen-'+state+'.png';image.alt='Dining room looking into kitchen with glazed divider '+state;link.href=image.src;note.textContent=state==='open'?'Panels fold at the rear end of the opening.':'Glazing separates the kitchen while retaining views.';document.querySelectorAll('[data-state]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)))}));</script></html>'''.replace('COMPARE',comparison).replace('FIGURES',figures).replace('ROWS',rows)
